{
 "facts": "deskline is a Node command-line tool for help-desk tickets, organised by technical layer (controllers, services, validators, formatters). Its README says the command line is the public interface. Planted in it: the list of priorities and what each one means is written in four files (the validator's list, a switch in slaService.js, a switch in ticketFormatter.js, and an ORDER list plus a second copy of the SLA hours in statsController.js), so adding a priority touches four folders; status checks against the strings open, pending and closed are scattered over services, formatter and stats; controllers and services reach into the store's _tickets and _users arrays directly, and show() repeats getTicket(); the current time is a module-level global in clock.js that services read; slaService.js and ticketService.js import each other; statsController.js swallows every error in its loop, so a ticket with an unknown priority silently drops out of the counts while still being included in total; unused code (utils/legacyExport.js, listUsers, findByEmail); one test only asserts that listing returns something; stats, show, create and the formatter have no tests. A real bug: create() reads input.prority (a typo), so the slaHours it prints is always 48 whatever the priority. Fixing it changes output.",
 "run": [
  "node",
  "src/cli.js"
 ],
 "tests": [
  "node",
  "--test"
 ],
